Z||000000||dans87gt||09-16-1999||01:44 PM||||I was driving my 87 GT on the highway and smoked the motor, it wedged a connecting rod between the block and the crankshaft(nice hole), so the motor locked-up. I was wondering if I have done any damage to my auto transmission when the motor locked-up, I was going around 55 MPH. I looked in the transmission pan and didn't see any metal. <P>P.S. Does anyone have a 2.8/3.1 block for sale?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-16-1999||04:16 PM||||you shouldn't have hurt the tranny much if any. It should have come out of TC lock as soon as the pressure dropped which should have been almost instantly. W/o tearing apart, or running, the tranny there is no way to be totaly certan. I'd say try it with the new motor and see. Odds are it's OK. Did the rear wheels lock up? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||dans87gt||09-17-1999||07:41 AM||||No the wheels didn't lock-up, so I was hoping that I didn't break anything. <BR>Thanks for the reply||||reg||1
